comic book call backs a subtle nod to  friendship and hidden messages to mom  every superhero needs a good costume and  you won't believe the secrets inside  these mcu ensembles no  no i don't think i will the hulk is  known for his iconic purple pants but  when hulk was introduced they were  actually blue it wasn't until 1962's  incredible hulk issue 4 that he earned  his barney tinted trousers it's not like  purple pants grow on trees there's only  one dillards that carries these it's all  the way downtown and now i have to  many depictions of the character in  popular culture since have had him  wearing the purple pants likely because  the color contrasts against his green  skin so well but marvel films have  largely shied away from having bruce  banner wearing lavender coloured  trousers nevertheless like wolverine's  x-men outfit luke cage's headband or  visions green and yellow marvel has been  open to making wink-wink jokes about the  garish colors that looks so good on the  splash page but not on a cinema screen  in 2008 the incredible hulk bruce and  betty ross are reunited and on the run  from thunderbolt ross when betty buys  some clothes for him  what it's a quick call back to the  characters comic book roots just enough  to put a smile on the faces of knowing  fans  scott lang slash ant-man and hope van  dyne wasp spent the second ant-man film  fighting avastar ghost with the film  being hope's formal introduction as a  hero ant-man and wasp are both obviously  named after insects and can shrink to  their size for super aerobic battling  alluded to by the costume department  crafting of their suits the head of a  wasp can be seen on hope's suit while  the head of an ant has depicted in scots  duds both insects even have visible  antennae making them both fun and  surprisingly accurate though some might  not take notice of what appears to be  typical superhero costume paneling both  suits shift to a different shape after  the pinch of portions making the details  clearly intentional it's a subtle  callback to the insects these heroes are  named after and as always one of those  things that once you become aware you'll  never be able to not see it  the first marvel disney plus series one  division was not only a lot of fun but  also subject to perhaps the highest  degree of fan dissection one moments i  really had fans talking was the  halloween costumes of wonder maximoff  scarlet witch and vision are you old red  riding hood  i'm a sokovian fortune teller  when wonder and vision showed off the  halloween costumes an all-new halloween  spooktacular sharp-eyed viewers  recognized the nods to their traditional  comic book appearance years before one  division became a reality elizabeth  olsen said on late night with seth  meyers that when she was cast she was  told she'd never have to wear the comic  book suit you know i i did ballet  growing up but that's not a confident  look in a 2021 interview with looper  however producer mary lovanos said olsen  was excited about the chance to include  the costume in the series in addition to  wonder and vision wearing their comic  book suits ralph boner pietro war quick  silver's comic book look wonder  envisions children in the sitcom  universe billy and tommy could also be  seen wearing halloween costumes alluding  to their comic book roots the inclusion  of all five comic book looks as  halloween costumes was a whimsical  thrill a nod to the source material and  perhaps a microcosm of the entire series  unique tone  in 2017 store ragnarok hulk bruce banner  learned some crucial info about where  he's been and what's been going on in  his life since he left the avengers at  the end of avengers age of ultron if he  wanted to know more about himself  however perhaps all he had to do was  look down in one scene bruce is wearing  what appears to be a duran duran shirt  remember he'd been forced to put on tony  stark's clothes after reverting to human  form put these on this is a tony's club  not only is a tea and sport coat combo  something less than zero era downey jr  would have worn but the shirt bears  artwork from the band's 1982 album rio  which produced the classic hungry like  the wolf at first it feels like a  throwaway bit of character development  that stark just happens to be a lover of  early 80s british new wave but the  t-shirt actually isn't truly dranjaran  related it just bears the same patrick  nagel artwork used on the album what's  the connection you might recall that  later in the film hulk has a key  smackdown with fenris a massive wolf who  runs alongside the evil heller some  marvel fans have concluded that the  stark shirt foreshadows that  confrontation but not so fast according  to ruffalo himself he was allowed to  select the robert downey jr referencing  wardrobe and the t is a reference to his  real life friend not a ragnarok plot  point in an interview to promote the  film ruffalo said i picked the things i  thought would be the most like downey jr  he loves duran duran they played at his  birthday party so i was like oh my god i  have to get the duran duran logo but i  couldn't get it so i got the nagel  instead  wonder vision and hulk are the only ones  who have been glimpsed in their comic  book looks at some point in the mcu in  2019's captain marvel carol danvers got  a similar shouts out to her comic book  look when carol asked monica rambo for  help deciding what color she should wear  several different designs are cycled  through before the duo decide on the  iconic red and blue suit the fun comes  in with three projected color  combinations spotted by eagle-eyed fans  definitely not the first is an all-red  version of the suit a cool bag to the  red miss marvel comic book outfit the  next attempt is black and gold  reminiscent of a miss marvel suit  moniker then changes the suit colours to  a green and grey ensemble reminiscent of  the marvel suit in the comics  mcu easter eggs don't have to reference  old comic books sometimes they call back  to beloved plot points from the other  films in the pages of marvel comics  there was a romantic relationship  between black widow slash natasha  romanov and hawkeye slash clint barton  in the mcu the two characters had  something more closely resembling a  strong friendship either way works here  we're still friends right since they're  not already at me that's first glimpse  in captain america the winter soldier  black widow wears an arrow necklace  although never explained the necklace  points to hawkeye resident archer of the  avengers she can later be seen wearing  the necklace in avengers end game the  easter egg was confirmed in 2021 when  marvel studios honcho kevin feige  confirmed on twitter that the necklace  was a nod to clint feige added that the  jewelry was suggested by black widow  actor scarlett johansson herself yes the  arrow necklace was scarlet's idea she's  been wearing it since captain america  the winter soldier  friends love to share clothes but it  isn't often that you find yourself  sharing an outfit with a raccoon unless  of course you're both guardians of the  galaxy keep an eye on everyone's  favorite interplanetary anti-heroes and  you'll notice that star  peter quill and rocket raccoon share a  scarf between guardians of the galaxy  volume 2 and avengers end game before  star-lord was turned to dust via the  thanos snap in avengers infinity war he  wore a red scarf the only guardians of  the galaxy character to survive the snap  was rocket so it makes for an especially  touching nod when the snarling super  raccoon pops up in avengers end game  wearing the same scarf the scarf  combined with rocket using his most  well-known comic book suit in the big  battle were fun incorporations of comic  book information in the film and we can  only assume that when quill came back  rocket was there to give him a scarf  back and maybe a hug  sometimes the mcu even inserts hints of  other comic book characters into its  costumes in avengers end game for  instance that's a little known reference  to somebody else who briefly became  captain america at least in the comics  when endgame steve goes back in time to  1970 to get the tesseract you can see  that the uniform he's wearing as a  disguise bears last name roscoe this  appears to be a reference to roscoe  simons in mid-70s captain america comics  simons was presented as a youngster who  was a huge fan of cap later captain  america would become nomad leaving his  moniker up for grabs as several  individuals attempted to fill the  position trained by falcon rasco simons  was one of these wannabe warriors  although his story had a sad ending at  the hands of the red skull and it seems  like it's not worth it  and you wonder  why you waited so long for something so  disappointing steve using that name as  his disguise in endgame is a nice nod to  the comic books as well as other people  that have served as captain america but  there is one problem with it the  military lists last names on uniforms  not first names so the reference should  read simon's  while fans may have been too distracted  by an age steve rogers at the end of the  film to pick up on it right away steve  was wearing a recognizable jacket after  going back in the timeline to replace  all the infinity stones it becomes clear  that captain america has altered the  plan where is he  i don't know he blew right by his time  stamp he should be here bucky barnes had  notices that steve is sitting nearby now  an old man having lived the entirety of  a life that had previously been stolen  from the thought out super soldier if  the jacket this old man is wearing looks  familiar that's because it's similar in  color and shape to the jacket he wore in  captain america the first avenger when  audiences first saw him with this look  it was before he became captain america  so it is meant to evoke a return to who  he was in those early scenes bringing  the jacket back in what is perhaps a  final appearance of chris evans cap in  the mcu helps his story come full circle  in black panther the costume department  gave a less than subtle nod to the  pan-african flag went to charles slash  black panther okay and nakia go to south  korea to try and intercept the sale of a  wakandan artifact by ulysses claw the  black market dealer some may recognize  from avengers age of ultron their  outfits stand out the three of them are  in the colors of the pan-african flag  t'challa in black okoye in red and nakia  in green this isn't the only time it  happens either throughout the film  t'challa wears black okoye wears red and  the kia wears green when they're  together and if you watch closely  they're typically lined up to maintain  the message the pan-african flag was  created by marcus garvey a jamaican  journalist and political activist in the  1920s garvey also founded the universal  negro improvement association and the  african communities league the flag is  used as a symbol of black nationalism  and was used as part of the black  liberation movement in the 1960s this  nod to a flag that is so important to  black americans is an excellent touch  eric killmonger stephen  jadaka comes to wakanda where he fights  against t'challa for the wakandan throne  as is his birthright he wins and  t'challa is presumed dead  nah  i'm your king when it's discovered that  t'challa is not dead and the dora  malaysia turns on kill manga he fights  them in a special suit similar to black  panthers a suit he wears has a leopard  prince that was referred to as a golden  jaguar in the comics killmonger has a  favorite pet leopard named prey this cat  is highly trained with more speed and  strength than a typical leopard the suit  may even foreshadow what happens to kill  manga in the film as the pet is also  killed in wakanda  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite mcu easter eggs are coming  soon subscribe to our youtube channel  and hit the bell so you don't miss a  single one  [Music]

